WHY IT IS RESTRICTED

This project sends automated requests to third-party services, including
PCGamingWiki, ProtonDB and Steam. It is written to be a considerate client: it
rate-limits itself, caches aggressively, prefers bulk APIs over per-page
requests, identifies itself honestly in its User-Agent, and does not attempt to
circumvent access controls it encounters.

Those properties are easy to remove and expensive for the operators of those
services if someone does. The restriction exists to discourage a modified copy
being pointed at them, not to hoard anything clever — there is nothing here a
competent developer could not write themselves.

If you want to use any of this, ask. The answer is likely yes for anything that
is not "run it at volume against someone else's website".


